{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/5892-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-wraith-the-oblivion-20th-anniversary-edition","id":5892,"title":"What do you want to see in Wraith: the Oblivion 20th Anniversary Edition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-08T07:27:40-08:00","id":5892,"title":"What do you want to see in Wraith: the Oblivion 20th Anniversary Edition?","content":"Post your thoughts about what you\u2019d lmike to see the Wraith developers put into the 20<sup>th</sup> Anniversary Edition. <br /> <br /> My wishlist:<ul><li>Rules for Ferrymen and Spectres.</li> <li>Advice for alternatives to Shadowguiding.</li> <li>A write-up of each Dark Kingdom and for the more notable of the Far Shores.</li> <li>Write-ups for all of the Guilds, describing how each is faring in the modern world.</li> </ul>I'd also like to get a \u201cSkinlands\u201d supplement for it:<ul><li>Rules for the Risen, done in a way that doesn\u2019t reference <b>Vampire</b>.</li> <li>Updated rules for mediums, necromancers, and projectors (e.g., the Benandanti)</li> <li>Write-ups for the various hunter groups described in <b>The Quick and the Dead</b> and <b>Mediums</b>, plus the major players featured in <b>Orpheus</b>. Make this one part recapitulation of <b>Wraith</b>\u2019s material on mortals who interact with the dead and one part an <b>Orpheus</b> redux, with translation notes for fitting the latter in with the former.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T07:56:54-08:00","id":5918,"title":"","content":"The results of the Sixth Great Maelstrom, the massive numbers of Risen that have (most likely) been returned to the Shadowlands and what the return of the Ferrymen and departure of Charon resulted in for Stygia and the other Kingdoms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T09:12:49-08:00","id":6006,"title":"","content":"1) Wraith represents the first 20th to be addressing a book that never got a revised edition. So one of the big things I want to see is a serious look at the mechanics of the game, which I would love to see for Dreaming as well. I know the 20th books are not meant to be major system overhauls, but at least bringing Wraith up to Revised era mechanics would be a pretty useful thing for me.<br /> <br /> 2) The impossible task of trying to incorporate Orpheus into Wraith proper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T09:26:06-08:00","id":6039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/5892-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-wraith-the-oblivion-20th-anniversary-edition?p=6006#post6006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) The impossible task of trying to incorporate Orpheus into Wraith proper.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure I won't be the only one, but I'd rather <i>not </i>see this, but I also don't want the Hunter, Mummy or Demon stuff to drift in too much, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T11:23:09-08:00","id":6170,"title":"","content":"Eh. Hunter, Mummy, and Demon have virtually no connection to Wraith (with the sole exception that when the hordes of newly-Risen found themselves stuck in the Skinlands after the Sixth Maelstrom began, they were confronted by the newly-Imbued hunters); so it makes quite a bit of sense not to say too much about any of them. OTOH, Orpheus was the spiritual successor to Wraith. And especially if you\u2019re going to be asking for post-Reckoning setting information, it makes sense to address it. At the very least, have entries for Orpheus and its rival corporations alongside the various pre-Maelstrom groups such as the Orphic Circle and the Alternate Energy Group, with Wraith-compatible mechanics for the company\u2019s projector technology alongside the Benandanti rituals for entering the Underworld. Not in the core book, mind you; that should focus primarily on the Shadowlands, with even the Risen being inappropriate due to their general isolation from the Shadowlands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T14:05:14-08:00","id":6319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/5892-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-wraith-the-oblivion-20th-anniversary-edition#post5892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Post your thoughts about what you\u2019d lmike to see the Wraith developers put into the 20<sup>th</sup> Anniversary Edition.<br /> <br /> My wishlist:<ul><li>Rules for Ferrymen and Spectres.</li> <li>Advice for alternatives to Shadowguiding.</li> <li>A write-up of each Dark Kingdom and for the more notable of the Far Shores.</li> <li>Write-ups for all of the Guilds, describing how each is faring in the modern world.</li> </ul><br /> I'd also like to get a \u201cSkinlands\u201d supplement for it:<ul><li>Rules for the Risen, done in a way that doesn\u2019t reference <b>Vampire</b>.</li> <li>Updated rules for mediums, necromancers, and projectors (e.g., the Benandanti)</li> <li>Write-ups for the various hunter groups described in <b>The Quick and the Dead</b> and <b>Mediums</b>, plus the major players featured in <b>Orpheus</b>. Make this one part recapitulation of <b>Wraith</b>\u2019s material on mortals who interact with the dead and one part an <b>Orpheus</b> redux, with translation notes for fitting the latter in with the former.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with all of this though I don't see all of it making it into the Rulebook, even with stretch goals. But would definitely want the rules for the Risen and Orpheus included in a manner more than just as passing mention. Something like the Changing Breeds in W20 Rulebook with a future supplement planned would be great.<br /> <br /> Write-ups on the other Dark Kingdoms and the Far Shores as well as an expanded write-up on the Guilds would make some great stretch goals. In fact I would love for them to do a Wr20 book just on the geography of the Underworld as well as either the missing Guild books or just one big Guild book covering them all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T14:08:35-08:00","id":6324,"title":"","content":"I\u00b4d like to have some material/rules from &quot;Spectres&quot; and &quot;Player\u00b4s guide&quot; or even &quot;Shadow guide&quot; in it. Since i heard the other 20th Anniversary editions had also expanded material inside.<br /> Maybe some streamlining on the Shadow but i realy hope they do not tone down the game\u00b4s gritty aspects at all. Think it should be as grim/dark as the first two editions. (yes i know there\u00b4s much hope in Wraith).<br /> Though i love and adore Orpheus the 20th Wraith wouldn\u00b4t need it at all imho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/709-nihil","name":"Nihil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar709_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T22:13:22-08:00","id":6630,"title":"","content":"For never having a revised edition, the majority of <i>Wraith</i>'s mechanics are relatively clear and precise. I'm speaking of just the core rulebook here, and <i>The Great War</i>. That being said, I would like to see the system updated to the <i>20th</i>-style, which will more than likely happen.<br /> <br /> As for included material, well... information from the <i>Player's Guide</i>, <i>Shadow Player's Guide</i>, <i>Haunts</i>, <i>The Sea of Shadows</i>, <i>Spectres</i>, and <i>Doomslayers</i> are essential, in my opinion. The Shadow and the Tempest being the most difficult subjects for players to grasp, in my experience. Putting together a <i>Wraith</i> &quot;bible&quot; for my own benefit, cutting out and collecting just the relevant sections from each of those books makes less than 500 pages when combined with the core book.<br /> <br /> I'd love to have the Risen included as well, but I don't think they're &quot;necessary&quot; for the setting. I'd also love to have a separate, huge Guildbook Compendium, including information on all the Guilds that never received a &quot;proper&quot; release. It could even just cut-and-paste the Mnemoi chapter from <i>Ends of Empire</i> and I'd be fine with that.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of alternative Shadow-play. I think we can all agree, the Shadow is something that really put off a lot of players, making it hard to get most people to even try the game.<br /> <br /> I'm one of the people who thinks <i>Orpheus</i> should not have anything to do with <i>Wraith</i>. I know and understand that they're intricately linked, but they're separate game lines, and, for me, I have absolutely zero interest in anything <i>Orpheus</i>.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","user":"nothing","date":". 11-09-2013, 01:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T23:48:34-08:00","id":6667,"title":"","content":"I can live without Orpheus. I would like to see rules for the Risen, the guilds and if this set post the Sixth Great Maelstrom a brief blurb on who now rules Syria as I recall from End of Empires that the Death Lords were all pretty much toasted. I'd like to see more of the mixed Arcanoi in the game as well as proper write-ups on the various other Dark Kingdoms but I could live with expansions/geography books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T01:34:27-08:00","id":6684,"title":"","content":"I agree about not putting Orpheus (the company, not the game) in the core book. I would also be against putting <i>any</i> of the hunter groups (e.g., Benandanti, Alternate Energy Group, etc.) in the core book: stuff that\u2019s focused primarily on what\u2019s going on in the Skinlands should have a separate book, akin to <b>Hunters Hunted 2</b>. And yes, that includes the Risen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T06:27:32-08:00","id":6780,"title":"","content":"Seriously guys... wraith 20? Are you nuts... the game is unplayable with Players trying to role play and other players constantly whispering at them. Unless shadow mechanics were completely revamped its not going to work. Ect roll for Shadow influence. ..this is what it says or does.... you feel/don't feel compelled by it. Any other way you could never play this game because its broken to hell...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/488-blackwood","name":"Blackwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar488_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T06:33:53-08:00","id":6781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/5892-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-wraith-the-oblivion-20th-anniversary-edition?p=6780#post6780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously guys... wraith 20? Are you nuts... the game is unplayable with Players trying to role play and other players constantly whispering at them. Unless shadow mechanics were completely revamped its not going to work. Ect roll for Shadow influence. ..this is what it says or does.... you feel/don't feel compelled by it. Any other way you could never play this game because its broken to hell...</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny how quite a few of us had great fun with it, playing it AS WRITTEN.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/373-infernal-teddy","name":"Infernal Teddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar373_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T06:44:11-08:00","id":6787,"title":"","content":"Well kudos. You did better than anyone I know who played and that's a fair few people","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/488-blackwood","name":"Blackwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar488_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T07:12:01-08:00","id":6796,"title":"","content":"To have the risen included into the core rulebook, i dont know why but they are my favorite thing in WoD<br /> <br /> I dont mind that they can lern disciplines, but said disciplines should be included with them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/122-talum","name":"Talum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar122_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T10:37:03-08:00","id":6910,"title":"","content":"Maybe some people should watch the lastest video-interviews the Gentleman Gamer did on Youtube with R.Dansky and M.R.Hagen.<br /> They also talk about Wraith and some minor changes, that would make the game more appealing....and about why this game seems to have more fans today than it did back then in the 90\u00b4s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/709-nihil","name":"Nihil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar709_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T11:40:37-08:00","id":6947,"title":"","content":"More info on Heretics and the Far Shores would be killer. My secret hope is for a Translation Guide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T14:29:27-08:00","id":7031,"title":"","content":"Since a Translation Guide would require something that it can be translated <i>to</i> (e.g., a nWoD Wraith line; Geist doesn\u2019t count), I\u2019m all in favor of this idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T15:23:20-08:00","id":7062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/5892-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-wraith-the-oblivion-20th-anniversary-edition?p=7031#post7031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since a Translation Guide would require something that it can be translated <i>to</i> (e.g., a nWoD Wraith line; Geist doesn\u2019t count), I\u2019m all in favor of this idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T20:03:51-08:00","id":7157,"title":"","content":"Besides all that has been said.<br /> <br /> - More about the Organization Hierarchy and a little about the Rebels.<br /> - Information about each Legion.<br /> - Data on the Organization of the Necropolis.<br /> - Show each major Heresies and how to create a data and quickly on Minor Heresies.<br /> - Malfeans, spectrum and other hazard.<br /> - Shades.<br /> - Mummies of the Wod: Mummy (and cultural variations).<br /> - Demons (from the Abyss): As in the Demon:TF main <span style=\"color:#009900\"><u>book</u></span> (I think) some strong demons could briefly extend their &quot;arms&quot; on the Underworld, trying to destroy the souls of the traitorous humans<br /> - The Wyrm, probably Eater of Souls (from the Abyss or Malfeas): As the demons, the Wyrm would probably be delighted of crushing human souls<br /> - Creatures from the <span style=\"color:#009900\"><u>Outer Space</u></span> (<u>from the Outer Space</u>): Doing it just because it's fun.All the Cthulhu-esque assumptions are contained","signature":"","edited":{"userid":641,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","user":"Ben Linus","date":". 11-09-2013, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T10:57:42-08:00","id":7498,"title":"","content":"I have a demand that can't be met; artwork just as stunning as the fantastic work that was in every Wraith book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T00:32:08-08:00","id":11942,"title":"","content":"Physically, I'd like the book to have black edging, like the <i>Sandman Omnibus</i>. Pic below.<br /> <img src=\"http://media.boingboing.net/wp-content/uploads/2013/09/tumblr_mt19ennKUQ1ry54nno3_12802.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Source: <a href=\"http://boingboing.net/2013/09/13/leatherbound-sandman-omnibus.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://boingboing.net/2013/09/13/lea...n-omnibus.html</a><br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T02:18:15-08:00","id":13288,"title":"","content":"I can definitely see Risen having a place in the Wraith20 book, given the detailed write-ups given to Ghouls, Revenants, and Kinfolk in Vampire and Werewolf.<br /> <br /> I imagine it'd be best, though, if anything on Orpheus were held off for a supplement. And if they do touch on all that again I think it would work better to rework/expand the Wraith mechanics rather than translate the old Orpheus stuff wholecloth. As much as I like the old Orpheus mechanics for what they were, they are definitely designed more for &quot;Orpheus as its own thing that ties in with Wraith&quot; rather than any sort of Wraith expansion. Mechanically, the old Horrors were just fine if you're just doing that, but guidelines on using Arcanoi with Orpheus operatives would be much more crossover-friendly if one wanted to focus more on the Wraith end of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Christopher Shaffer, freelancer. Game line contributions: W20, Night Horrors, TC: \u00c6on, Scion (details <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2019/07/stuff-ive-worked-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>) <br /> <a href=\"http://mythicfoxwrites.blogspot.com/2020/10/actual-play-index.html\" target=\"_blank\"> <b>Blog post write-ups of my gaming sessions; Currently running Exalted, and also updating old Promethean sessions</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/171-mythicfox","name":"MythicFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar171_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T06:30:21-08:00","id":13357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/5892-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-wraith-the-oblivion-20th-anniversary-edition?p=13288#post13288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can definitely see Risen having a place in the Wraith20 book, given the detailed write-ups given to Ghouls, Revenants, and Kinfolk in Vampire and Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main difference between including Risen in the core Wraith20 book and including ghouls, revenants and kinfolk in vampire and werewolf is that the ghouls, revenants, and kinfolk can interact with vampires and werewolves with ease; whereas the Risen have essentially exiled themselves from the Shadowlands, where most or all of the action in a <b>Wraith</b> game takes place. They\u2019re in the same boat as mediums and the mortals found in <b>The Quick and the Dead</b> and <b>Mediums: Speakers With the Dead</b>, and should only be included in the core if mediums and ghost hunters are also included in the core. Which <i>is</i> a possibility; but I think that the line would be better served with the denizens of the Skinlands getting their own supplement. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythicFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/5892-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-wraith-the-oblivion-20th-anniversary-edition?p=13288#post13288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine it'd be best, though, if anything on Orpheus were held off for a supplement. And if they do touch on all that again I think it would work better to rework/expand the Wraith mechanics rather than translate the old Orpheus stuff wholecloth. As much as I like the old Orpheus mechanics for what they were, they are definitely designed more for &quot;Orpheus as its own thing that ties in with Wraith&quot; rather than any sort of Wraith expansion. Mechanically, the old Horrors were just fine if you're just doing that, but guidelines on using Arcanoi with Orpheus operatives would be much more crossover-friendly if one wanted to focus more on the Wraith end of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>What to do with Orpheus largely depends on what <b>Wraith 20</b> does with the Sixth Maelstrom. Because the line was ended with the coming of the ghost-storm, the writers could easily ignore it altogether, in which case, Orpheus could easily be handled with a footnote somewhere to the effect of \u201cthere\u2019s this corporation in the Skinlands called Orpheus that\u2019s dabbling in \u2018necro-science\u2019, but nothing has come of it yet; see <b>Orpheus</b> (available on DTRPG) for more information.\u201d OTOH, if <b>Wraith 20</b> facilitates chronicles that take place after the coming of the ghost-storm, then real thought should be put into presenting Orpheus and its projectors in a manner that\u2019s compatible with <b>Wraith</b> (e.g., replacing Horrors with Arcanoi), to be included or excluded at the Storyteller\u2019s whim.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T20:25:35-08:00","id":13753,"title":"","content":"I'd personally love to see more on Heretics. I mean, we had Book of Legions, The Hierarchy and Renegades, but I felt Heretics were lacking info (aside from what was scattered here and there, chiefly in Players Guide if I remember correctly).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1082-nfi","name":"NFI","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T00:47:34-08:00","id":15211,"title":"","content":"An effort to incorporate some of Orpheus with Wraith would be good, in my eyes. Aside from that I would be keen to see the rules get an upgrade and a larger, expanded and more playable world to run around in. Focus in the core book on more necropoli than just Stygia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T17:39:35-08:00","id":15739,"title":"","content":"Indeed. While Orpheus's overall plot is dependent on the 6GM, which obviously hasn't happened yet in Wr20, the company, its rivals as well as the Flatliners already existed chronologically before that. So why wouldn't the Orpheus Group and the other companies have some kind of impact on the Shadowlands?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-26T02:55:39-08:00","id":18316,"title":"","content":"I'd like to second Heavy Arms. Wraith seriously needs a re-work of mechanics. It also really needs expanding of the other Kingdoms and the societies and death rituals of those kingdoms. Not everything can possibly be set up the same as the &quot;Western Way&quot;. Just because Charon set things up that way doesn't mean it's been static for everyone all this time globally. The descriptions of history and culture of the other nations and wraiths are very Americanized. In trying to do research for making a Euthanatos Agama ritual, I found all KINDS of death rites and shadow culture in India I wish was in some of the Wraith books. China and Africa have very long histories of Ancestor worship too that would make profound impacts on the power struggles of the Shadowlands. Those Kingdoms would actually probably be much more dominant in the setting than any of the Wraith material would have us believe.<br /> <br /> There are rules for Ferrymen and Specters, but it could stand to be added to more.<br /> <br /> Blackwood: Yes, it is kinda broken. Very bleak. When you've had a recent death in the family IMPOSSIBLE to play and not be depressed as all hell and have to quit. But, that doesn't mean that we should let it remain that way. Now's the chance to make changes and improvements and flesh it out more into a world we can handle and play with hope without the annoying distractions and ladling the angst on with a trowel just to be true to the setting. Besides, if we don't support the making of Wraith20, why should Onyx bother making Changeling 20 or Hunter 20? Wraith is my least favorite classic 5 game of WW's because of all the holes in it. I'll gladly support the chance to make it something better.<br /> <br /> Back to what I'd like to see:<br /> <br /> <br /> Crossover rules. I for one like mixing up my games here and there. I try and completely understand each setting so that should a Mage embark on a Death journey, there's a world they go into, not just a subliminal holodeck in the Umbra. If Werewolves descend into the Spiral, why not have them pop out of the Black Labyrinth? If a Ferryman travels to the Far Shining Shores with his charges, might they not wind up in Faerie? If a Giovanni rips the Specter from a dying man, how might it act? What do the Legionaries do when the ephemeral prison for a Demon cracks? How does a Risen deal with a Hunter of Judgement when their target is the same person? I crave to have these options and some guidelines for adding more depth to my games. The world is so big, let's play in All of it, or at least have the option.<br /> <br /> Shadowlands is described in Werewolf as the Low umbra... it'd be nice to have some sort of reference back to the Rest of the Umbra or how Wraiths perceive spirits of other things, if they can perceive them at all. It might be out of their reach or even perception until they finally cast off all of their Fetters, but it seems to be that Wraith's setting for all its universal geography is very Very narrow. For some reason I keep thinking that the Shadowlands should be like Silent Hill or movies like The Others or Constantine's visions of Hell, and yet Wraith's material doesn't really speak to me of those visions. More spooky haunted house and quiet graveyards or battlefields of the dead. Not really visual to me until you get into descriptions of areas that might as well be knock offs of other descriptions like Malfeas or Blood Dimmed Tides.<br /> <br /> Atamajakki: How about artwork less John Cobb and more like Stephen Gammell? I personally think the Wraith artwork could have been better even when they did have Timbrook.<br /> <br /> Nothing: I think that's a fantastic idea!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> How about for the heck of it as a stretch goal: A cardstock Ouija board to go with the storyteller's screen. Why not? Bad taste? Mage had its own Tarot Deck. even New Mage has a Tarot deck.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T16:03:11-08:00","id":21334,"title":"","content":"Ola All,<br /> <br /> <u>My Wish List</u><br /> <br /> I. <u>Structural Changes</u><br /> - Rule Updates: Plain and simple, update the present rules to the newest version of the OWOD standard.<br /> <br /> - Rule consolidation: I think the present Wraith rules are great. My party has always had a wonderful time with them. I would simply consolidate material from various books into the same chapter/setting. Examples would be rules for travel in the tempest and or naval warfare. We have material in the main book, Sea of Shadows, Dark Kingdom of Jade, Wraith the Great War, etc... for ship to ship combat and varied aspects of tempest travel. I would be nice to see them in one place. The same concept applies to the varied thorns for shadows and specter abilities.<br /> <br /> - Translation guide for the NWOD (I run my present Wraith game in the NWOD and plain and simple, its a huge amount of fun. Its not even that difficult to translate over.<br /> <br /> <br /> II. <u>Material to Add</u><br /> - Information on the Heretics (as the poster above mentioned, we have a hierarchy book, book of legions and renegade book. It would be great to get a little more color on the Heretics.<br /> <br /> - Additional material on the remaining guilds that did not receive treatment in the guildbook series (Harbringers in particular).<br /> <br /> - Expanded information on the Dark Kingdom of Ivory along with unique arcanoi/merits/relics/artifacts for Ivory Kingdom characters.<br /> <br /> - More sample artifacts/relics and perhaps a set of creation guidelines.<br /> <br /> - Ceremonies/rituals for wraiths to perform (similar to those in the Book of the Dead from the NWOD)<br /> <br /> - Legion/hierarchy symbols and rank insignia (mask styles, Stygian and Shadowlands version of sigils of rank and office).<br /> <br /> - Blood Potency/Primal Urge/Synergy style merit/background to differentiate old ghosts from new (I just call it &quot;Psyche&quot; and basically use a hybrid of the Blood Potency system from the NWOD and the Synergy merit from Geist (aka, a gaunt with 3 fetters can have up to 100 points of pathos and spend 15 a turn...is this common...no...but it differentiates a death lord from the average wraith on the street).<br /> <br /> - Expanded color on the shining ones and/or far shores (I draw on the Book of the Dead for sample far shores). I like the concept of going &quot;rivers deep&quot; through the tempest to travel to particular far shores, etc.<br /> <br /> - Random encounter table for the tempest/labyrinth.<br /> <br /> - A little more rule info on dark steel weapons/armor.<br /> <br /> - When it comes to extra bling, I would go for some type of oboli counters or maybe a Stygian seal of citizenship ring or other wax seal with the symbol of the hierarchy.<br /> <br /> - A new sample necropolis and starter adventure. Even something along the lines of how the cities are treated in Wraith the Great War would be very helpful.<br /> <br /> - Per The Gentlemen Gamer's interview with Richard Dansky, some sample adventure ideas/adventures that represent that different aspects of the Wraith world and how it can be played (high fantasy, personal horror/resolve fetters, light hearted/Beatlejuiceish, quest for transcendence, etc...)<br /> <br /> III. <u>Material to Omit </u><br /> - I would hold off on Orpheus with the possible exception of importing some of their more unique specter variants into the antagonist section as example villains. I think there is quite a bit to unpack here and that it deserves a book of its own. Maybe a mention similar to the Orphic Circle or the Giovanni with some light rules for sleepers, etc. Shouldn't be too tough.<br /> <br /> - I would go light on the crossover mechanics. About a quarter page should suffice like the NWOD. I love me some antagonists and mortal foes/necromancers are great, but I think going too far beyond the ones presented in the 2nd Edition main book would detract from the setting. Wraith is Wraith and I think the setting has such a staggering amount of variety and diversity already without getting too deeply embroiled in the affairs of the living. It should be fairly easy to cross it over as is and I think more rules for plasmics or specters would better serve the setting.<br /> <br /> - I would say no Ouija board because they are more closely tied to mediums as opposed to wraiths themselves. I like the idea of going with oboli or a seal of citizenship as above (although dressed up death certificates like that off the old game would be great too).<br /> <br /> Aeoris","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The Mercy of Order is Justice&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1391-aeoris","name":"Aeoris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T16:13:17-08:00","id":21344,"title":"","content":"Wraith is my absolute favorite WOD game! Aeoris, I agree with all of your suggestions for additions and omissions! Would love to see those wax Hiearchy and/or citizenship seals and Oboli. Citizenship papers would be very cool too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1343-khaleesi","name":"Khaleesi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T14:58:57-08:00","id":331505,"title":"","content":"The main things I think Wraith always needed were A) more things tying the PCs to each other (e.g., some group chargen system/mechanic ensuring, say, common passions and fetters), and B) more things explicitly tying PC motivations to plot hooks in the source books.<br /> <br /> Even if all the players were good at coming up with fetters &amp; passions that translated well to usable story ideas, it was easy to wind up with a list of many goals everyone wanted to tackle, very few of which the PCs shared in common, and most of which could only be approached through highly-demanding roleplay (which is great, but, well, highly demanding). Then the source books gave us tons of setting detail which, even when I could translate them into usable plot hooks, could still be hard to tie to the various personal motivations which are necessarily the center of a wraith's universe.<br /> <br /> Directing players to a list of common fetters and/or passions (in a more or less draconian way, as far as the char gen mechanics go) may make it easier to publish material with plot hooks that are likely to hook them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4448-bphillips","name":"bphillips","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T15:10:49-08:00","id":331517,"title":"","content":"To give an example to what bphillips just said:<br /> <br /> I once ran a really good WtO one-shot game at a convention. One of the reasons I could do this is because I pre-made all the characters (with enough and a variety to make sure my players got to pick from a selection), tying all of their Passions and Fetters together (some more obviously than others) and to the set up I put together.<br /> <br /> This made things very smooth because they all had obvious reasons to work on a common goal without a lot of time spent making all of them mesh together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T21:34:49-08:00","id":331896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/5892-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-wraith-the-oblivion-20th-anniversary-edition?p=331517#post331517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To give an example to what bphillips just said:<br /> <br /> I once ran a really good WtO one-shot game at a convention. One of the reasons I could do this is because I pre-made all the characters (with enough and a variety to make sure my players got to pick from a selection), tying all of their Passions and Fetters together (some more obviously than others) and to the set up I put together.<br /> <br /> This made things very smooth because they all had obvious reasons to work on a common goal without a lot of time spent making all of them mesh together.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the very first bits of writing I did for WW was an article for Inphobia on keeping your wraiths together. I suspect it could use some updating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T22:08:59-08:00","id":331930,"title":"","content":"We know there is going to be incentive to be guild member this time<br /> <br /> 1 - Hopefully that will include Arcanoi powers that are Guild Secrets.<br /> <br /> 2 - Hopefully the game will not forsake Legions and Heretics as player options. The Legions deserve some incentive as well, and Heretics never got deep coverage before the original line ended... and on that point...<br /> <br /> 3 - Coverage of interesting Far Shores","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T23:56:03-08:00","id":332004,"title":"","content":"I'd love some wordcount on Heretics and the Far Shores. Always felt like Wraith was missing a book on those two.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T01:48:32-08:00","id":332058,"title":"","content":"What I want to see:<br /> <br /> Detailed writeups of all the Guilds, especially the ones who never got a Guildbook.<br /> Updated Arkanoi, with both new and familiar Arts.<br /> A detailed section on the other Dark Kingdoms, with a focus on making them playable.<br /> Material from Dark Reflections, the Players Guides, Doomslayers and the Hierarchy and Renegade books.<br /> A detailed write-up of the Heretics faction, which never got a book of their own.<br /> <br /> But most importantly, I want the game to be preserved like it was and is. I don't want any changes to the setting, especially not in the name of making the game more accessible.<br /> Please, no Guilds as splats. Please. Wraith doesn't need splats.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4449-eisenkreutzer","name":"EisenKreutzer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4449_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T03:50:28-08:00","id":332100,"title":"","content":"This may be an unpopular opinion but... I wouldn't mind seeing a little bit of color in this book. (Jumps behind the nearest solid object)<br /> <br /> Just a little bit here and there could make the book look really great, even if it is still mostly black and white.<br /> <br /> New arts, or things that can be done with the arcanoi.<br /> <br /> More info on Drones... where they can be found, what they do, are they rare, are they common? Can their behavior be influenced at all? What happens if they are prevented from re-enacting their deaths? What happens after they are done? What makes them fall to oblivion? can they be made sentient?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T06:48:16-08:00","id":332181,"title":"","content":"Everything a ST could possibly need on Specters, Renegades, Mediums and artifacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T07:56:36-08:00","id":332220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/5892-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-wraith-the-oblivion-20th-anniversary-edition?p=332100#post332100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may be an unpopular opinion but... I wouldn't mind seeing a little bit of color in this book. (Jumps behind the nearest solid object)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there are gonna be color art, it is mentioned a few times <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> but it is going to be thematic colors on how thing looks in the Shadowlands, so no bright happy pappy colors <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1159-kjetilkverndokken","name":"kjetilkverndokken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1159_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T07:58:49-08:00","id":332221,"title":"","content":"With the Orpheus and Guidebook for New wraiths . . . I am not certain what new stuff I want?<br /> <br /> If the guidebook does not delve into it, I want a good portion of articles focussing on the interactions with the Skinlands and those that are alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1159-kjetilkverndokken","name":"kjetilkverndokken","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1159_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T08:06:19-08:00","id":332224,"title":"","content":"There's a few thing I would love to see in Wraith 20th.<br /> <br /> - First: I want to see more about the &quot;Mnemosynis&quot; Arcanoi as well as more about the Mnemoi Guild. Their official coverage left me...wanting.<br /> <br /> - Second a &quot;crossover&quot; covereage between Wraith and the Cappadocian/Giovani/Harbingers of Skulls (and Kaymakli and maybe Derinkuyu) as well as the Tal'mahe'Ra (and the City of Enoch)<br /> <br /> - Third another &quot;crossover&quot; coverage between Wraith and Werewolf...The Labyrith and Dark Umbra.<br /> <br /> - Fourth a &quot;Dark Age&quot; Wraith Coverage...something (like for Mummy) that was sadly missing in the DA line. As the Underworld was probably quite different between the First Maelstrom (Fall of Rome 470) and the Second Maelstrom (the Black Plague of 1342) than in Modern Night between the 5th and 6th.<br /> <br /> - Fifth a Necropolis From around the world book. to cover such spot at Istanbul, Paris, Rome, Herculanum/Pompeii/Stabiae/Oplontis/Boscoreale, etc.<br /> <br /> -A Demon/Wraith crossover (if there is a link) and an update on the Quick and the Dead could be nice too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":3226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","user":"Boneguard","date":". 12-15-2014, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T10:19:11-08:00","id":332269,"title":"","content":"Historical settings are my number one at this point; it's all Wraith is missing for me. And please mention that Wraiths all speak the same language.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T15:51:07-08:00","id":332525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/5892-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-wraith-the-oblivion-20th-anniversary-edition?p=332269#post332269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Historical settings are my number one at this point; it's all Wraith is missing for me. And please mention that Wraiths all speak the same language.</div> </div> </div> </div>They do? huh<br /> <br /> I thought that was one of the reason people tended to stick near the Necropoli.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T15:57:43-08:00","id":332527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/5892-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-wraith-the-oblivion-20th-anniversary-edition?p=332525#post332525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They do? huh<br /> <br /> I thought that was one of the reason people tended to stick near the Necropoli.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, it's stated in the core book (I think) that &quot;the language of death is universal.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4449-eisenkreutzer","name":"EisenKreutzer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4449_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T16:29:35-08:00","id":332565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EisenKreutzer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/5892-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-wraith-the-oblivion-20th-anniversary-edition?p=332527#post332527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, it's stated in the core book (I think) that &quot;the language of death is universal.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the opening fiction of Wraith: the Great War has the wraith of a British soldier freeing a newly dead German soldier from his caul, saving him from an oncoming storm front and the two of them taking seeking refuge from it with a third wraith *cough* Charon *cough*. There they explain some of the things wraithly nature, including despite coming from different countries with different languages they can understand each other. The dead are able to speak a shared language.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T22:34:15-08:00","id":332760,"title":"","content":"I'm assuming language barriers still apply to understanding the Quick?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-07T01:09:54-08:00","id":332859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/5892-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-wraith-the-oblivion-20th-anniversary-edition?p=332760#post332760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm assuming language barriers still apply to understanding the Quick?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, language of death may be universal but languages of the living are a multitude.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T13:12:29-08:00","id":334489,"title":"","content":"This may be a bit heretical, but\u2026<br /> <br /> I\u2019m inclined to want to see some of the innovations from <b>Orpheus</b> integrated into <b>Wraith</b>, particularly the Shades: in <b>Wraith</b> terms, these would serve as splats that represent psychological predispositions and manifest as affinities for particular Arcanoi. They would <i>definitely</i> parallel some of the Guilds, in that a given Guild would seek to recruit and train wraiths who show a natural aptitude for their chosen craft. The irony is that if the Dictum Mortuum is still in force, the very Guilds who would be suited to recruiting by Shade would generally be the ones who have been driven furthest into the shadows by that law. <br /> <br /> I\u2019d also like to see an Appendix that deals with the Sixth Great Maelstrom and its effects, taking cues from <b>Hunter: the Reckoning</b> and <b>Orpheus</b> as well as <b>End of Empire</b>. The usual game wouldn\u2019t operate under the 6GM assumptions; but it would be there for those who want to play a more apocalyptic take on <b>Wraith</b>, where the society of the Dead has been shattered and the survivors have been forced to deal with the Living whether they want to or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T14:26:21-08:00","id":334541,"title":"","content":"Now, I know cWoD is less crossover-friendly by design, but I would like there to be a discussion in the book of the various supernatural others and the sort of influence they have in the Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> -Can they see or hear wraiths?<br /> -Can they converse, or physically touch wraiths?<br /> -Can they cross the shroud? How?<br /> -Can they go to the tempest or deeper?<br /> -Are these beings prone to taking an interest in the shadowlands? Why?<br /> <br /> Rules-wise, this may be asking for a lot since some of the 20th anniversary editions haven't come out yet, but getting the low down and dirty mechanics-wise would be great. &quot;In Mage terms, to get to the shadowlands, a mage needs these spheres...&quot; just so that we don't have to go book hunting to answer the question &quot;Could a mage show up in the Shadowlands?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T14:58:17-08:00","id":334563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/5892-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-wraith-the-oblivion-20th-anniversary-edition?p=334489#post334489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may be a bit heretical, but\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>It ain't heretical to me. I love both lines and more than welcome such an idea. Honestly I haven't heard the 'Orpheus is an insult to WtO' or 'Orpheus is poor imitation of WtO' or whatever complains in <i>years</i>. Even with the KS and the Orpheus stretch goal I haven't heard any complaints about including Orpheus with Wr20.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-08T15:00:34-08:00","id":334567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/5892-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-wraith-the-oblivion-20th-anniversary-edition?p=334541#post334541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I know cWoD is less crossover-friendly by design, but I would like there to be a discussion in the book of the various supernatural others and the sort of influence they have in the Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> -Can they see or hear wraiths?<br /> -Can they converse, or physically touch wraiths?<br /> -Can they cross the shroud? How?<br /> -Can they go to the tempest or deeper?<br /> -Are these beings prone to taking an interest in the shadowlands? Why?<br /> <br /> Rules-wise, this may be asking for a lot since some of the 20th anniversary editions haven't come out yet, but getting the low down and dirty mechanics-wise would be great. &amp;quot;In Mage terms, to get to the shadowlands, a mage needs these spheres...&amp;quot; just so that we don't have to go book hunting to answer the question &amp;quot;Could a mage show up in the Shadowlands?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of this has been covered before, actually. Vampires need Necromancy to do anything with Wraith and the Shadowlands, the Euthanatoi and the Void Engineers can visit the Shadowlands, and the Halaku have a ton of powers revoling around Wraith stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T06:49:39-08:00","id":370955,"title":"","content":"Other things I'd like to see... A sampling of relics with costs in oboli. Does this already exist somewhere? Would it be as easy as adding a note to the end of each level of the Relics background, e.g.:<br /> <br /> * (Standard writeup followed by...) A relic in this category can usually be purchased for an eighth (1/8 obolus).<br /> ** (Standard writeup followed by...) A relic in this category can usually be purchased for a half-obolus.<br /> ...etc.<br /> <br /> I'm totally guessing at costs because I have no idea what an obolus is worth.<br /> <br /> Maybe the costs should be listed as &quot;X oboli or Y pathos&quot;? I feel like the pathos-containing artifacts (soulfire crystals? I can't recall) should condense pathos into a liquid visible inside and have notches so you can see how many pathos are in there. Then pathos could be used as currency too without taking a Usurer's word for things, assuming an abundance of such artifacts. The anti-soul-smelting crowd would insist on it, right? (How big is that crowd, anyway? Just a few hippy heretics here and there?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4448-bphillips","name":"bphillips","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T06:53:52-08:00","id":370966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bphillips</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/5892-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-wraith-the-oblivion-20th-anniversary-edition?p=370955#post370955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the costs should be listed as &quot;X oboli or Y pathos&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>On second thought, I'd just list the costs in oboli and mention a probable pathos-to-obolus conversion rate somewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4448-bphillips","name":"bphillips","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T15:04:48-07:00","id":450916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/5892-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-wraith-the-oblivion-20th-anniversary-edition?p=334563#post334563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It ain't heretical to me. I love both lines and more than welcome such an idea. Honestly I haven't heard the 'Orpheus is an insult to WtO' or 'Orpheus is poor imitation of WtO' or whatever complains in <i>years</i>. Even with the KS and the Orpheus stretch goal I haven't heard any complaints about including Orpheus with Wr20.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, I suspect that most people in the KS weren't envisioning Orpheus\u2019 inclusion in Wraith in the integrated manner I\u2019m considering. Most probably were thinking that Orpheus material would be safely confined to an appendix where it could be ignored by those not interested in it. And rightly so; I suspect that's what will happen. By contrast, what I'm thinking of would be a bit more invasive: Orpheus\u2019 Nature Groups would be integrated directly into Wraith\u2019s section on Natures, and <i>all</i> wraiths would have to pick a Shade: Every wraith would now be a Banshee, Haunter, Poltergeist, Skinrider, Wisp, Phantasm, Marrow, or Orphan Grinder, with innate biases toward certain Arcanoi and certain Nature Groups. <br /> <br /> That's not just tacked-on optional information; that's a significant change from how the earlier editions work. I think that Wr20 would benefit from this, which is why I suggested it; but it would still be a big change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T18:11:10-07:00","id":451121,"title":"","content":"i was thinking..it would be nice if the Delux Edition had some metal casting to make Oboli","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T19:06:37-07:00","id":451181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/5892-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-wraith-the-oblivion-20th-anniversary-edition?p=450916#post450916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, I suspect that most people in the KS weren't envisioning Orpheus\u2019 inclusion in Wraith in the integrated manner I\u2019m considering. Most probably were thinking that Orpheus material would be safely confined to an appendix where it could be ignored by those not interested in it. And rightly so; I suspect that's what will happen. By contrast, what I'm thinking of would be a bit more invasive: Orpheus\u2019 Nature Groups would be integrated directly into Wraith\u2019s section on Natures, and <i>all</i> wraiths would have to pick a Shade: Every wraith would now be a Banshee, Haunter, Poltergeist, Skinrider, Wisp, Phantasm, Marrow, or Orphan Grinder, with innate biases toward certain Arcanoi and certain Nature Groups.<br /> <br /> That's not just tacked-on optional information; that's a significant change from how the earlier editions work. I think that Wr20 would benefit from this, which is why I suggested it; but it would still be a big change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that is what they said they'd do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At <b>$130,000</b> of contributions, we will take the current <b>Orpheus </b>sub-section of the <b>Wraith 20th Anniversary Edition</b> book and expand it into its own Appendix, fully fleshing out <b>Orpheus</b> to work within the <b>Wraith 20th </b>setting. This is a big addition to the project and will add at least 15,000 words and rearrange the book- but it'll be worth it! </div> </div> </div>Though as fan of both lines I wouldn't mind hearing more of what you had in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T23:31:01-07:00","id":451339,"title":"","content":"A simple list of Anime/Books/Films/Music as sources of stylistic/thematic inspirations for those who are new to telling the Ghost Story Genre.<br /> Hopefully Patrick Swayze's &quot;Ghost&quot; and &quot;Brandon Lee's &quot;The Crow&quot; will make the cut for that list :RIP Both Gentlemen. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T16:58:37-07:00","id":453364,"title":"","content":"Considering <i>Risen</i> was basically <i>The Crow: The Roleplaying Game</i>, it better make the cut.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}